14:["$","h2","b3458",{"id":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What to know before you pick"]}]
15:["$","ul","b3460-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3460",{"children":["Real product or invented look? Garment fidelity and creative range pull against each other, and no tool here wins both."]}],["$","li","b3462",{"children":["Fabric is the tell. Drape, weight and sheen under moving light are what separate a campaign clip from an obvious generation."]}],["$","li","b3464",{"children":["Identity drift across clips ruins a set faster than any single clip's quality, so test the second and third clip, not the first."]}],["$","li","b3466",{"children":["Check commercial rights before anything runs as paid media, and check them per tool, because they differ."]}]]}]
16:["$","h2","b3468",{"id":"what-separates-a-good-fashion-video-tool","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["What separates a good fashion video tool?"]}]
17:["$","p","b3470",{"children":["Four criteria, and the first one eliminates most general-purpose video models for real product work."]}]
18:["$","h3","b3472",{"children":["The garment stays the garment"]}]
19:["$","p","b3474",{"children":["A generated clip that subtly redesigns your jacket is worse than useless, because it advertises something you don't sell. Watch the details that carry a garment's identity: the neckline, the seam lines, the hardware, the print placement. These are what drift first, and they drift more the longer the clip runs."]}]
1a:["$","h3","b3476",{"children":["The same model across every clip"]}]
1b:["$","p","b3478",{"children":["A campaign is a set, and a set needs one person in it. Identity drift is the failure that makes an AI campaign read as AI, because a viewer notices the face changed between the story and the feed post even when they can't say why. Look for a reference or character mechanism instead of re-prompting a description each time."]}]
1c:["$","h3","b3480",{"children":["Fabric under moving light"]}]
1d:["$","p","b3482",{"children":["Stills forgive material errors that motion exposes. Silk that doesn't catch light as it moves, denim with no weight, knitwear that behaves like plastic: all of it reads instantly to anyone who works in fashion. Test your hardest material, not a cotton t-shirt."]}]
1e:["$","h3","b3484",{"children":["Motion that reads as editorial"]}]
1f:["$","p","b3486",{"children":["Fashion has its own camera language, and it's mostly restrained: a slow push, a locked-off frame, a single deliberate move. Tools that default to swooping drone energy produce something that looks like AI video rather than like a campaign. Control over the camera matters more here than in most categories."]}]
20:["$","h2","b3488",{"id":"the-five-compared","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["The five compared"]}]
21:["$","div","b3489",{"role":"region","aria-label":"Comparison table, scroll horizontally to see all columns","tabIndex":0,"data-lenis-prevent":true,"className":"my-10 max-w-full overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-white shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-orange","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-left","children":["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","b3490",{"className":"bg-black/[0.04]","children":[["$","td","b34900",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3493",{"children":[["$","strong","b3492",{"children":["Tool"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b34901",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3496",{"children":[["$","strong","b3495",{"children":["Best at"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b34902",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3499",{"children":[["$","strong","b3498",{"children":["How it holds the garment"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b34903",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3502",{"children":[["$","strong","b3501",{"children":["Consistency across clips"]}]]}]]}],["$","td","b34904",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-gray-dark-1 px-4 py-3 font-medium","children":[["$","p","b3505",{"children":[["$","strong","b3504",{"children":["Free tier"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3506",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b35060",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3509",{"children":["Melius"]}]]}],["$","td","b35061",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3512",{"children":["Building the whole campaign set in one workflow"]}]]}],["$","td","b35062",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3515",{"children":["Your own stills as reference nodes, per-step model choice"]}]]}],["$","td","b35063",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3518",{"children":["5/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b35064",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3521",{"children":["Yes, limited trial credits, all models"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3522",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b35220",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3525",{"children":["Runway"]}]]}],["$","td","b35221",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3528",{"children":["Cinematic control and in-house frontier models"]}]]}],["$","td","b35222",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3531",{"children":["Image-to-video from your own frame"]}]]}],["$","td","b35223",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3534",{"children":["4/5"]}]]}],["$","td","b35224",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3537",{"children":["Yes, a one-time starting credit allowance"]}]]}]]}],["$","tr","b3538",{"className":"border-t border-black/10","children":[["$","td","b35380",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3541",{"children":["Higgsfield"]}]]}],["$","td","b35381",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3544",{"children":["Camera moves and human motion"]}]]}],["$","td","b35382",{"className":"t-b-3 min-w-48 align-top [&_p]:m-0 text-foreground px-4 py-3.5","children":[["$","p","b3547",{"children":["Image-to-video with motion presets"]}]]}],"$L5d","$L5e"]}],"$L5f","$L60"]}]}]}]
22:["$","h2","b3587",{"id":"1-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["1. Melius"]}]
23:["$","p","b3589",{"children":["Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: you describe the campaign and an agent builds the workflow, routes each step to the right model, and leaves every step editable. A node-based canvas sits underneath, so the whole pipeline from garment still to finished cut is visible and re-runnable, though plenty of people drive it from Slack and never open the canvas."]}]
24:["$","p","b3591",{"children":["For fashion the advantage is that a campaign is a set of related outputs, and a canvas is the natural shape for that. One approved look feeds the hero cut, the social variants and the product page loop as branches of the same graph, not three separate jobs you do three times."]}]
25:["$","h3","b3593",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
26:["$","ul","b3595-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3595",{"children":["Two fashion templates ship in the product: fashion campaign video for an editorial look, and high-end fashion commercial for a studio scene built from model and garment photos."]}],["$","li","b3597",{"children":["Fabric and texture analysis reads an input garment and writes the expert prompt for manipulating it, which is the step most people get wrong by hand."]}],["$","li","b3599",{"children":["Per-step model routing, so the model that renders fabric isn't the one asked to carry the motion."]}],["$","li","b3601",{"children":["References and character nodes carry one look across every clip in the set."]}],["$","li","b3603",{"children":["Storyboard turns a single image into a 9-panel sequence, which is a fast way to agree a campaign's shape before generating video."]}],["$","li","b3605",{"children":["Multiplayer, so the art director and the producer work on the same canvas instead of trading exports."]}]]}]
27:["$","p","b3610",{"children":["The model routing is what makes this practical rather than theoretical. Melius publishes its own per-job guidance and it splits fashion work across models deliberately: material, fabric and editorial lighting go to one, faces and character consistency to another, cinematic motion to a third. Because the whole ",["$","$L61","b3608",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3607","href":"/models","isNewTab":false},"children":["library of leading models"]}]," sits on one subscription, the agent can use all three inside a single workflow instead of making you pick a favourite and live with its weak side."]}]
28:["$","p","b3612",{"children":["The catch: this is a workflow tool, so the first campaign takes longer to set up than typing a prompt into a single-model app. The payoff arrives on the second campaign, when the graph is already built."]}]
29:["$","p","b3614",{"children":["Best for: brands and agencies producing a campaign set, not one clip, who want the look agreed once and then applied across every cut."]}]
2a:["$","h2","b3616",{"id":"2-runway","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["2. Runway"]}]
2b:["$","p","b3618",{"children":["Runway's approach has been to build its own frontier video models instead of reselling everyone else's. Its Gen-4 line is exclusive to the platform, which is the strongest single argument for paying for it."]}]
2c:["$","p","b3620",{"children":["It's also the most film-literate tool here. The controls assume you know what a camera does, and the output rewards that knowledge, which suits fashion work more than the consumer-shaped alternatives."]}]
2d:["$","h3","b3622",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
2e:["$","ul","b3624-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3624",{"children":["In-house frontier models you can't get anywhere else, alongside access to several third-party models on one plan."]}],["$","li","b3626",{"children":["Genuine camera and motion control, not a preset menu."]}],["$","li","b3628",{"children":["Strong image-to-video, which is how most fashion campaign work actually starts."]}],["$","li","b3630",{"children":["A mature editing surface around the generation, so clips get assembled and not merely produced."]}],["$","li","b3632",{"children":["Long-established use in professional film and advertising work, which makes craft knowledge easy to find."]}]]}]
2f:["$","p","b3634",{"children":["Credits go fast at the good settings, and the frontier model is the expensive one, so users report a real campaign on Runway costing more than the headline plan price suggests. It also gives you no help with garment accuracy specifically: it's a general video model, and it will happily redesign your jacket while making a beautiful clip."]}]
30:["$","p","b3636",{"children":["The catch: budget by the clip rather than by the month, and expect to regenerate."]}]
31:["$","p","b3638",{"children":["Best for: teams with film instincts who want maximum control and are willing to pay for the frontier model."]}]
32:["$","h2","b3640",{"id":"3-higgsfield","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["3. Higgsfield"]}]
33:["$","p","b3642",{"children":["Higgsfield's angle is motion, specifically camera motion. Where most tools ask you to describe a shot, Higgsfield gives you named moves to apply to a still, which turns out to be a fast and reliable way to get a clip that looks directed instead of drifting."]}]
34:["$","p","b3647",{"children":["For fashion that's more useful than it sounds. A locked-off frame with one deliberate push is most of what campaign video needs, and getting there by picking a move beats getting there by prompt archaeology. We've written separately on ",["$","$L61","b3645",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3644","href":"/blog/higgsfield-alternative","isNewTab":false},"children":["Higgsfield alternatives"]}],"."]}]
35:["$","h3","b3649",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
36:["$","ul","b3651-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3651",{"children":["Named camera moves applied to a still, which is the fastest route to a directed-looking clip."]}],["$","li","b3653",{"children":["Human motion and fabric behaviour, which Higgsfield attributes to a team background in computer vision and biomechanics."]}],["$","li","b3655",{"children":["A low entry price relative to the frontier platforms."]}],["$","li","b3657",{"children":["Quick iteration, so testing several moves on one garment still is cheap."]}],["$","li","b3659",{"children":["Good results from a single input image, with no reference set required."]}]]}]
37:["$","p","b3661",{"children":["The preset approach is also the ceiling. Once you want a move that isn't in the menu, or a longer cut with more than one beat, you're working against the tool. Consistency holds reasonably well inside one preset and slips when you mix them across a campaign set."]}]
38:["$","p","b3663",{"children":["The catch: it's a clip generator, not a campaign system, so assembly and versioning happen somewhere else."]}]
39:["$","p","b3665",{"children":["Best for: getting a good-looking single clip out of a strong still, quickly and cheaply."]}]
3a:["$","h2","b3667",{"id":"4-kling","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["4. Kling"]}]
3b:["$","p","b3669",{"children":["Kling is the pick when a person has to move convincingly. Its handling of body mechanics, weight and gait is among the best available, and it holds up at higher resolutions than most of the field, which matters if the clip is going anywhere bigger than a phone."]}]
3c:["$","p","b3671",{"children":["It shows up in fashion work often for exactly that reason. A walk that reads as a real walk is most of a campaign clip's credibility."]}]
3d:["$","h3","b3673",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
3e:["$","ul","b3675-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3675",{"children":["Realistic human movement, above all walking and full-body motion."]}],["$","li","b3677",{"children":["High output resolution relative to the category."]}],["$","li","b3679",{"children":["Solid image-to-video from a single model shot."]}],["$","li","b3681",{"children":["Reference support for holding a subject across clips."]}],["$","li","b3683",{"children":["Available on several platforms besides its own, including Melius."]}]]}]
3f:["$","p","b3685",{"children":["The tooling around Kling is thinner than the model deserves. There's no brand system, no campaign structure, and the interface assumes you're making one clip at a time. It's also the entry where checking which version you're actually getting matters most, because platforms reselling it don't all expose the same one."]}]
40:["$","p","b3687",{"children":["The catch: a strong model with light workflow around it, so plan on assembling the campaign elsewhere."]}]
41:["$","p","b3689",{"children":["Best for: clips where the model's movement is the thing the viewer will judge."]}]
42:["$","h2","b3691",{"id":"5-wearview","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["5. WearView"]}]
43:["$","p","b3693",{"children":["WearView is the specialist, and on its own narrow job it beats every general tool here. It's built for fashion e-commerce: virtual try-on, AI model creation, ghost mannequin work, and short fashion video generated from the product shots you already have."]}]
44:["$","p","b3695",{"children":["The reason to consider it over anything else on this list is garment accuracy. Its own documentation describes animating flat-lays, ghost mannequins and model shots while holding the same model and the same garment across clips, which is precisely the problem general video models don't solve."]}]
45:["$","h3","b3697",{"children":["What it does well"]}]
46:["$","ul","b3699-parent",{"children":[["$","li","b3699",{"children":["Purpose-built for real garments, so the clothing is treated as a fixed input, not something to reinterpret."]}],["$","li","b3701",{"children":["Movement templates such as a catwalk walk or a 360 degree spin, which covers most product-page video needs."]}],["$","li","b3703",{"children":["Ghost mannequin and flat-lay inputs, meaning you don't need on-model photography to start."]}],["$","li","b3705",{"children":["Same model and garment held across a set of clips, per its documentation."]}],["$","li","b3707",{"children":["Commercial usage rights on paid plans, which its own pages state plainly."]}]]}]
47:["$","p","b3709",{"children":["The narrowness cuts both ways. For a brand campaign with invented scenes, art-directed lighting and a mood that isn't a product spin, WearView has far less range than any of the general models, and you'll hit its edges quickly. It's also a much smaller company than the rest of this list, which is worth weighing if this becomes core infrastructure."]}]
48:["$","p","b3711",{"children":["The catch: excellent inside e-commerce fashion video, limited outside it."]}]
49:["$","p","b3713",{"children":["Best for: fashion e-commerce teams animating real SKUs for product pages and paid social."]}]
4a:["$","h2","b3715",{"id":"building-a-campaign-set-on-melius","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Building a campaign set on Melius"]}]
4b:["$","p","b3717",{"children":["Begin with one good garment still and the fashion campaign video template for an editorial look, or high-end fashion commercial if you're building a studio scene from model and garment photos. Run fabric and texture analysis on the input first: it writes the prompt for handling that specific garment, which is the step most people get wrong by hand."]}]
4c:["$","p","b3725",{"children":["Hold the look with references and character nodes rather than re-describing the model each time, because description-based consistency drifts by the second or third clip. The agent splits the work across models deliberately, sending fabric and editorial lighting one way, faces and character consistency another, and cinematic motion a third. Storyboard turns a single frame into a 9-panel sequence, which is the cheapest way to agree a campaign's shape before you generate any video. The same ",["$","$L61","b3720",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3719","href":"/blog/brief-to-execution-workflow","isNewTab":false},"children":["brief-to-execution workflow"]}]," applies to the ",["$","$L61","b3723",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3722","href":"/blog/best-ai-image-generators-marketing","isNewTab":false},"children":["marketing image side of a campaign"]}],"."]}]
4d:["$","p","b3727",{"children":["The honest limit is long takes. Flowing fabric across 20 continuous seconds, or hands touching clothing, is still where a real shoot is cheaper than the retries."]}]
4e:["$","h2","b3729",{"id":"frequently-asked-questions","className":"scroll-mt-28","children":["Frequently asked questions"]}]
4f:["$","div","b3730",{"className":"faq-list my-10 flex flex-col divide-y divide-black/10 border-y border-black/10","children":[["$","details","0",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["What is the best AI tool for fashion campaign videos?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"It depends on whether the garment is real. For actual products you sell, a fashion-specific tool like WearView protects garment accuracy better than any general model. For brand campaign work with invented scenes, Runway gives the most cinematic control and Kling the most convincing human movement. Melius is the pick when you need a whole campaign set built once and re-run, because the look is agreed on a canvas and applied across every cut."}]]}],["$","details","1",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Can AI keep the same model across a whole campaign?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Yes, if you use a reference or character mechanism instead of re-describing the person in each prompt. Description-based consistency drifts, and the drift shows up by the second or third clip. On Melius, references and character nodes are reused across every clip in the set, and Kling and Runway both support reference images for the same purpose."}]]}],["$","details","2",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["How long can an AI-generated fashion video be?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"M6 9l6 6 6-6","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round"}]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-foreground-muted m-0 pr-8 pb-5","children":"Most useful campaign output is 5 to 10 seconds per clip, and longer cuts are assembled from several generations, not produced in one pass. Plan the campaign as a set of short beats you edit together, because a single continuous 30 second generation is where garment and identity drift become obvious."}]]}],["$","details","3",{"className":"faq-item","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"t-b-1 text-gray-dark-1 flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 font-medium select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":["Will AI video keep my garment accurate?",["$","svg",null,{"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","aria-hidden":"true","className":"text-foreground-muted size-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 [[open]_&]:rotate-180","children":"$L62"}]]}],"$L63"]}],"$L64","$L65","$L66"]}]
50:["$","p","b3735",{"children":["Start from the fashion campaign video template with one garment still, then branch it into the ratios and cuts your channels need. ",["$","$L61","b3733",{"link":{"_type":"link","_key":"b3732","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true},"children":["Open Melius"]}],"."]}]
51:["$","section","related",{"className":"relative w-full pb-section bg-gray-background","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"color":"gray"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-300 px-5 lg:px-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"t-h-2 mb-12 text-center text-balance text-gray-dark-1","children":"Related Articles"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto grid w-full max-w-max grid-cols-1 gap-11 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","$L67","post-best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts",{"post":{"_key":"post-best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","slug":"best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts","category":"comparisons","title":"Best tools for AI generated design concepts","isoDate":"2026-09-05","date":"September 5, 2026","readTime":"10 Min Read","excerpt":"Five AI tools for generating design concepts, compared on how precisely you can set a direction, comparing options, and reusing a look later.","image":{"url":"/images/blog/best-tools-ai-generated-design-concepts/cover.webp"},"authors":[{"name":"Melius Team"}],"faq":[{"question":"What is the best AI tool for design concepts?","answer":"Match it to the discipline: Midjourney for the loosest visual exploration, Vizcom for physical product concepts from sketches, Recraft for identity and vector systems, and Melius when the approved direction has to be reapplied across a body of work. Kosmik is the one to add if your problem is research and not generation."},{"question":"Can AI generate design concepts that are actually usable?","answer":"Yes at the direction stage, less so as finished work. These tools are strong at proposing and resolving a look and weak at the precision a production asset needs, so the realistic use is to settle the direction with AI and finish in your normal tools. Treat the output as a concept, which is what it's good at."},{"question":"How do I keep a concept consistent once it's approved?","answer":"Capture the direction as something reusable instead of one image. A written style description, a saved style, or a brand kit can all be reapplied months later; a single lucky generation cannot. On Melius the approved direction stays as a node you re-run against new inputs, which is the same idea made concrete."},{"question":"Is Midjourney still the best for concept art?","answer":"For range and aesthetic quality it's still the one most designers reach for first, and style references have made it much more directable. Its weaknesses are everything after the idea: brand control, legible text, exact palettes and getting a look out of Midjourney and into real assets. There's also no free tier, so you can't test it against your references before paying."},{"question":"Do I need to be able to draw to use AI concepting tools?","answer":"No for graphic and brand concepting, and it helps a lot for product concepting. Vizcom is built around a sketch and rewards being able to make one, while the others take a written direction or a reference set. If you can't draw, working from references instead of from a blank prompt gets you much closer."},{"question":"Do I own concepts I generate with AI?","answer":"It varies by tool, so check before a concept goes into client work. On Melius you own what you create and can use it commercially, subject to the underlying model providers' terms, and Melius does not use your work to train AI models. Read the terms per tool, because free consumer tiers are the ones most likely to restrict commercial use."},{"question":"Will AI concepting replace art direction?","answer":"No. Generating options is now nearly free, which makes choosing between them the scarce skill and no longer the easy part. The judgment about which direction is right for this brand and this audience is the work, and these tools remove the labour around that decision, not the decision itself."}],"tableOfContents":[{"_key":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-design-concepts","title":"Which AI tool should you use for design concepts?"},{"_key":"what-to-know-before-you-pick","title":"What to know before you pick"},{"_key":"what-separates-a-good-concepting-tool","title":"What separates a good concepting tool?"},{"_key":"the-five-compared","title":"The five compared"},{"_key":"1-melius","title":"1. Melius"},{"_key":"2-midjourney","title":"2. Midjourney"},{"_key":"3-vizcom","title":"3. Vizcom"},{"_key":"4-recraft","title":"4. Recraft"},{"_key":"5-kosmik","title":"5. Kosmik"},{"_key":"from-approved-concept-to-finished-asset","title":"From approved concept to finished asset"},{"_key":"frequently-asked-questions","title":"Frequently asked questions"}],"content":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3737","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3736","text":"Which AI tool should you use for design concepts?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"which-ai-tool-should-you-use-for-design-concepts"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3739","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3738","text":"Choose based on what you're concepting, because the tools that win product design and the tools that win brand direction are barely in the same category. A physical product needs a sketch turned into something buildable. A campaign direction needs a look you can defend in a room and then reproduce. Those are different problems.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3741","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3740","text":"The trap in this category is judging tools on whether the output is beautiful. At the concept stage beauty is cheap and abundant. What's scarce is a direction specific enough to brief against, and a look that survives when you apply it to the next twelve assets.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3743","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3742","text":"What to know before you pick","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-to-know-before-you-pick"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3745","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3744","text":"Concepting and rendering are separate jobs. Exploring twenty directions and resolving one of them reward different tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3747","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3746","text":"A direction you can write down is worth more than one you stumbled into, because only the written one is briefable.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3749","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3748","text":"You'll generate far more than you present, so how fast you can compare and discard matters as much as output quality.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3751","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3750","text":"Check whether the concept can travel. A look trapped in one tool's session is a look you'll rebuild later.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3753","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3752","text":"What separates a good concepting tool?","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"what-separates-a-good-concepting-tool"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3755","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3754","text":"Four things, and the last one is the one people discover too late.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3757","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3756","text":"How precisely you can set a direction","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3759","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3758","text":"There's a wide gap between picking minimal from a menu and specifying a warm neutral palette, soft top light from camera-left, matte ceramic surfaces and a shallow depth of field. The second is what lets you match an existing brand or an art director's reference. Judge a tool on how much of that it will actually listen to.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3761","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3760","text":"Comparing directions side by side","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3766","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3763","href":"/blog/best-ai-creative-canvases-image-generation","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3762","text":"Concepting is divergent by nature: you make five directions to kill four. A tool that shows you one output at a time forces you to hold the comparison in your head, which is where good options get lost. Being able to branch a direction and see the alternatives together is worth more than a marginally better single image, which is the argument for a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3764","text":"node-based creative canvas","marks":["b3763"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3765","text":".","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3768","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3767","text":"Whether the look survives to the next asset","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3770","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3769","text":"A concept's job is to be applied. If the approved direction exists only as one lucky image, somebody has to reverse-engineer it for every asset that follows. A look captured as a reusable style, a written description or a saved configuration is one you can still apply in three months.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3772","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3771","text":"Getting to something you can present","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3774","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3773","text":"Concepts get shown to people who didn't make them, which means a raw generation is rarely the deliverable. Mockups, placements, a board that reads as considered: the tools differ a lot on how much of that they'll do, and it's usually the difference between a concept being approved and being misunderstood.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3776","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3775","text":"The five compared","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"the-five-compared"},{"_type":"portableTable","_key":"b3777","rows":[{"_key":"b3778","cells":[{"_key":"b3779","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3781","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3780","text":"Tool","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3782","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3784","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3783","text":"Concepting it suits","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3785","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3787","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3786","text":"How you set a direction","marks":["strong"]}]}]},{"_key":"b3788","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3790","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3789","text":"Reusable afterwards","marks":["strong"]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3791","cells":[{"_key":"b3792","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3794","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3793","text":"Melius","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3795","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3797","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3796","text":"Brand, campaign and asset direction","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3798","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3800","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3799","text":"Style analysed from a reference, or written out","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3801","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3803","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3802","text":"Yes, as a node you re-run","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3804","cells":[{"_key":"b3805","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3807","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3806","text":"Midjourney","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3808","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3810","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3809","text":"Mood, visual exploration, concept art","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3811","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3813","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3812","text":"Style references and moodboards","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3814","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3816","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3815","text":"Partly, via style references","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3817","cells":[{"_key":"b3818","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3820","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3819","text":"Vizcom","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3821","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3823","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3822","text":"Physical product and industrial design","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3824","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3826","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3825","text":"Your own sketch, plus material prompts","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3827","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3829","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3828","text":"Yes, models carry into computer-aided design","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3830","cells":[{"_key":"b3831","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3833","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3832","text":"Recraft","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3834","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3836","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3835","text":"Brand identity, icons and vector systems","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3837","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3839","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3838","text":"Brand kits and style presets","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3840","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3842","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3841","text":"Yes, styles are saved and reapplied","marks":[]}]}]}]},{"_key":"b3843","cells":[{"_key":"b3844","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3846","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3845","text":"Kosmik","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3847","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3849","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3848","text":"Visual research before you generate anything","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3850","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3852","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3851","text":"You collect it, and it surfaces adjacents","marks":[]}]}]},{"_key":"b3853","text":[{"_type":"block","_key":"b3855","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3854","text":"Yes, the board is the artefact","marks":[]}]}]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3857","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3856","text":"1. Melius","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"1-melius"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3859","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3858","text":"Melius is the Agentic OS for creative work: describe the direction you're chasing and an agent builds the workflow, picks the right model per step, and leaves every step editable. A node-based canvas underneath turns a concept into a graph you can branch, compare and re-run.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3861","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3860","text":"That shape suits concepting unusually well. Five directions become five branches off one reference instead of five separate sessions, and the one that gets approved is already a working configuration you point at the next asset.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3863","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3862","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3865","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3864","text":"Image style analysis reads a reference image and describes its style, which turns somebody's moodboard into something briefable.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3867","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3866","text":"Sketch to image resolves a rough drawing into realistic detail, so a napkin idea becomes presentable without redrawing it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3869","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3868","text":"Brand anchor holds palette, type and rules as a node, so concepts stay inside the brand instead of drifting out of it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3871","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3870","text":"Branching on the canvas puts competing directions side by side instead of one after another.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3873","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3872","text":"Storyboard turns a single image into a 9-panel sequence, which is a quick way to show a direction as a narrative.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3875","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3874","text":"Multiplayer, so the review happens on the work, not in a separate thread of screenshots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3880","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3877","href":"/models","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3876","text":"The style-analysis step is the one that changes the work. Most concepting dies at the handoff, where an approved image has to become a brief that somebody else can execute against. Reading the style out of the reference as text closes that gap: the direction becomes words you can argue with, edit and reapply, not a vibe attached to one file. Behind it sits a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3878","text":"library of leading models","marks":["b3877"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3879","text":", so the model that analyses a reference isn't the one asked to render the concept.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3882","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3881","text":"The catch: the payoff is in the reuse, so for a single one-off concept you'll feel the setup cost without collecting the benefit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3884","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3883","text":"Best for: brand and campaign concepting where the approved direction has to be applied across a body of work.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3886","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3885","text":"2. Midjourney","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"2-midjourney"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3888","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3887","text":"Midjourney is still the default for visual exploration, and among art directors and brand designers it's the one that gets opened first. Its output has a point of view, which sounds like a criticism and is actually the reason it works for concepting: it proposes things you wouldn't have asked for.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3890","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3889","text":"Style references and moodboards have made it considerably more directable than it used to be. You can hand it a set of images and get work in that register, which is the mechanism most concepting workflows now hang off.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3892","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3891","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3894","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3893","text":"An aesthetic range that proposes directions you would not have thought to specify.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3896","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3895","text":"Style references let you steer toward an existing look without training anything.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3898","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3897","text":"Moodboards build a persistent personal aesthetic you can generate against.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3900","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3899","text":"Genuinely fast divergent exploration, which is the core concepting motion.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3902","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3901","text":"A very large community, so the craft knowledge is easy to find.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3904","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3903","text":"It remains weak at everything after the idea. Precise brand control, legible text, exact palettes and structured output are all outside what it's trying to do, and there's no free tier to test it against your own references first. Concepts also tend to stay in Midjourney: getting an approved look applied to real assets means rebuilding it somewhere else.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3906","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3905","text":"The catch: unmatched at proposing directions, unhelpful at executing them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3908","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3907","text":"Best for: the earliest, loosest stage, when you want range rather than control.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3910","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3909","text":"3. Vizcom","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"3-vizcom"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3912","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3911","text":"Vizcom is the tool here built for physical products, and if that's what you design it's not really competing with the rest of the list. It takes an industrial designer's sketch and renders it, keeping the geometry you drew instead of reinterpreting it into something merely similar.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3914","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3913","text":"The reason it matters is that product concepting has a downstream that graphics work doesn't. A concept has to become a model somebody engineers, and Vizcom sends work toward computer-aided design instead of stopping at a pretty picture.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3916","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3915","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3918","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3917","text":"Sketch to render that respects your linework instead of redrawing it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3920","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3919","text":"Material and finish exploration on a fixed form, which is exactly how product concepting iterates.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3922","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3921","text":"3D output, with a path into Autodesk Fusion for the engineering handoff.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3924","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3923","text":"Adaptive Canvas removes fixed aspect-ratio limits mid-project.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3926","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3925","text":"Unify composites a design into a real environment with matched lighting, for validation shots.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3928","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3927","text":"Outside physical product design it's the wrong tool, and it doesn't pretend otherwise. There's no brand system, no campaign thinking, and no reason to reach for it if your concepts are graphics, layouts or campaign imagery. Its pricing has also moved around, so check its own pricing page rather than a third-party tracker.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3930","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3929","text":"The catch: superb at one discipline, irrelevant to the others.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3932","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3931","text":"Best for: industrial, product and packaging designers working from sketches toward something manufacturable.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3934","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3933","text":"4. Recraft","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"4-recraft"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3936","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3935","text":"Recraft performs best when the concept has to be a design system, not an image. It generates true vectors, editable in Illustrator or Figma, which means a logo or icon concept arrives as something a designer can actually finish, not a raster to trace.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3938","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3937","text":"For brand concepting the brand kit is the useful mechanism. Colours, style preferences and identity parameters are stored and applied across everything you generate, so a set of concepts holds together instead of each one being its own accident.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3940","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3939","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3942","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3941","text":"True scalable vector graphics output, editable downstream in standard design tools.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3944","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3943","text":"Brand kits that carry colour and identity parameters across a whole set of concepts.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3946","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3945","text":"Style presets you can define once and reapply, which keeps a system coherent.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3948","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3947","text":"Strong at icons, illustration and the flat graphic work most AI tools handle badly.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3950","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3949","text":"A low paid entry point relative to what it does.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3952","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3951","text":"It's narrower than it looks. Photoreal imagery, campaign scenes and anything cinematic are not what Recraft is for, and reviewers rate its raster output as unremarkable next to the frontier models. Treat it as the vector and identity specialist, not a general concepting tool.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3954","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3953","text":"The catch: brilliant inside vector and brand-system work, ordinary outside it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3956","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3955","text":"Best for: identity, icon and illustration concepts that need to survive into production files.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3958","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3957","text":"5. Kosmik","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"5-kosmik"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3960","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3959","text":"Kosmik is on this list as the honest counterweight: it generates nothing. It's a spatial canvas for visual research, where you collect images, PDFs, video and live web pages, and it surfaces related material and organises what you've gathered.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3962","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3961","text":"It earns the slot because a lot of what people call concepting is really research, and doing that badly is why generated concepts come out generic. Feeding a model a considered reference set produces better work than feeding it a sentence, and this is a tool for building the reference set.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3964","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3963","text":"What it does well","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3966","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3965","text":"An infinite spatial canvas that holds mixed media, including live web pages, in one place.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3968","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3967","text":"Surfaces related visual material from something you've uploaded, so research compounds.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3970","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3969","text":"Auto-organises a growing reference library instead of leaving you to file it.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3972","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3971","text":"The board itself is the deliverable, which suits a direction review well.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3974","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3973","text":"A 1-week free trial, enough to build a first board and see whether the habit sticks.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3976","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3975","text":"If you need an image made, this is not the tool, and pairing it with a generator is the actual workflow. It's also a smaller product than the rest of this list, which matters if it becomes where your reference library lives.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3978","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3977","text":"The catch: it improves the input to concepting rather than doing the concepting.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3980","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3979","text":"Best for: art directors and brand designers whose reference libraries have outgrown a folder of screenshots.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3982","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3981","text":"From approved concept to finished asset","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"from-approved-concept-to-finished-asset"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3984","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3983","text":"The handoff is where concepting work usually leaks, and it's worth planning for before you start, not after a direction is signed off.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3986","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3985","text":"The failure looks like this: a concept gets approved as a single image, the person who made it moves on, and everyone downstream reverse-engineers the look from that one file. Palette drifts, the type is a near-miss, and three assets in, nobody can say what the direction actually was. The concept was never written down, so it couldn't be applied.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3991","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3988","href":"/blog/best-ai-image-generators-marketing","isNewTab":false}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3987","text":"Avoiding it is mostly a matter of capturing the direction as something other than an image: a written style description, a saved style, a brand kit, a configuration you can re-run. Tools differ on whether they let you do that, and it's the criterion that separates a concepting tool from a nice image generator. If a look can only exist as one output, treat the concept as unfinished. The same discipline is what makes ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3989","text":"marketing image generation","marks":["b3988"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3990","text":" survive past the first asset.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3993","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3992","text":"Frequently asked questions","marks":[]}],"anchorId":"frequently-asked-questions"},{"_type":"faqList","_key":"b3994","items":"$51:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:post:faq"},{"_type":"block","_key":"b3999","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_type":"link","_key":"b3996","href":"https://app.melius.com","isNewTab":true}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"b3995","text":"Drop a reference image on the canvas, run image style analysis to turn it into a written direction, then branch it into the concepts you want to compare. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3997","text":"Open Melius","marks":["b3996"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"b3998","text":".","marks":[]}]}]}}],"$L68","$L69"]}]]}]]}]
